{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4105577a-7dd1-4bbb-a7d3-e575d382c61f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-94236cfd69c18bc9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-sjigf84f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E001.md","content":"# Validate mid-run availability of status.benchmarks[] in the EvalHub job detail API\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves whether the EvalHub Server's job detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populates the `status.benchmarks[]` array — per-benchmark status entries with `started_at`/`completed_at` — while a job is still running, or only after completion. The strategy's benchmark-level progress display (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") and mid-run elapsed-time computation depend on this answer. The strategy explicitly flags this as an open question owned by the TrustyAI / EvalHub team (\"needs validation\"), and Staff Engineer direction constrains the solution to data already available from the existing API.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the EvalHub Server source (upstream repository, evaluation-jobs status handling) and the published API reference for `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}` to determine when `status.benchmarks[]` entries are written relative to job state transitions (pending → running → completed/failed).\n- Determine whether per-benchmark `started_at` is available before the first benchmark completes (needed for mid-run elapsed time).\n- Where source reading is inconclusive, empirically observe the detail-endpoint response for a running evaluation job (may require a live cluster running an evaluation job).\n- Deliverable: a short findings report stating (a) whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated mid-run, (b) which per-benchmark fields are present at each job state, and (c) the recommended display consequence: benchmark-progress display as planned, or the strategy's fallback (elapsed time as primary progress indicator, benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written findings report answers, with evidence (source file references and/or captured API responses): \"Is `status.benchmarks[]` populated with per-benchmark status entries while a job is still running, or only after completion?\"\n- The report states which fallback (if any) the EvalHub UI progress display must adopt.\n- The TrustyAI / EvalHub team and the ODH Dashboard team sign off on the conclusion.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-1 [P0] (auto-refresh with detail-endpoint progress data), HLR-4 [P1] (benchmark-level progress display), HLR-5 [P1] (elapsed time from per-benchmark `started_at`) — the answers determine whether these are implemented as specified or degraded per the strategy's risk fallback.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":44942,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af589b60cf509813","agent_id":"a76d34cd3e2df0381","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"b1ab20e0-2986-48fc-9690-f572f3f1973c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:54:23.619Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
