{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-225ae8a1-30f7-4a79-8fa1-e63ad5305f43","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb121aec328dca00","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-sjigf84f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E002.md","content":"# Catalog status.message.message_code values for pre-start vs runtime evaluation job failures\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation catalogs the values the EvalHub Server returns in `status.message.message_code` for job failures, and determines whether they reliably distinguish pre-start failures (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource/quota constraints) from runtime failures (failures after execution has started). The strategy's optional pre-start vs runtime failure distinction (\"Failed (not started)\" vs \"Failed\") depends on this answer; the strategy explicitly flags it as an open question owned by the TrustyAI / EvalHub team (\"needs validation\").\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the EvalHub Server source for all sites that write `status.message.message_code` and enumerate the distinct values with their triggering conditions (admission, scheduling, quota, runtime errors).\n- Cross-check against the published API reference for the job list and job detail endpoints.\n- Where source reading is inconclusive, reproduce representative failure scenarios (may require a live cluster, e.g., quota-exceeded admission failure vs a failing benchmark runtime).\n- Deliverable: a catalog table of `message_code` values mapped to failure phase (pre-start vs runtime), plus a verdict: distinguishable, partially distinguishable, or not distinguishable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A written catalog enumerates the known `status.message.message_code` values and the failure phase each indicates.\n- A clear verdict states whether the EvalHub UI can reliably render \"Failed (not started)\" distinct from \"Failed\" (runtime), including any ambiguous or absent-code scenarios.\n- If the verdict is negative, the strategy's documented fallback is confirmed as the path: a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message.message` text displayed as supplementary detail.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Enables HLR-7 [P2] (pre-start vs runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available) — the answer determines whether that feature is implemented or the fallback applies.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45691,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af589b60cf509813","agent_id":"a76d34cd3e2df0381","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"a21ff520-335c-428b-8266-86fa12a7c7e9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:54:35.591Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
