{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-126b0a9c-84e9-45ac-b06b-1e81b2764cbf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-80cdf30d663d9436","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-sjigf84f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E004.md","content":"# Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the progress presentation for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps. It renders the data delivered by the detail-polling layer in the job table rows.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs: \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"`.\n- Elapsed time display: computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (or `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started); formatted for display (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n- Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n- Per the strategy's risk mitigation, elapsed time is the primary progress indicator for all jobs (covering single-benchmark jobs where X/N is too coarse); the benchmark count is supplementary.\n- State-cell/table-row layout changes to present progress alongside the state badge, following PatternFly progress and label components and the UX-specified progress indicator pattern.\n- UX review of the progress indicator pattern (UXD support is listed as required for this in the strategy's prerequisites).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n- For a single-benchmark job, the running state with elapsed time provides progress feedback (risk mitigation acceptance).\n- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed and approved by UX/design against the dashboard design system.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 [P1]: Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (display half; the max-5 round-robin fetch is delivered by the detail-polling layer).\n- HLR-5 [P1]: Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps obtained via detail polling.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Depends on the detail-polling layer (its UI renders data delivered by that hook and its round-robin scheduling).\n- Gated by the investigation of mid-run `status.benchmarks[]` availability: if benchmark data is only populated on completion, this epic is rewritten to the strategy's fallback — elapsed time (from `resource.created_at` or list-endpoint data) as the primary progress indicator with the benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47564,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af589b60cf509813","agent_id":"a76d34cd3e2df0381","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"610be351-8d1f-47ae-b152-e99f8d73ddfa","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:55:14.793Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
