{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-18df19be-5feb-4939-ac23-c212d7dd2f78","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-995e592b240ec0d9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-sjigf84f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E006.md","content":"# Pre-start vs runtime failure state distinction\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the optional distinction between jobs that failed before execution started (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource constraints) and jobs that ran and then failed, using `status.message.message_code` where available. It extends the state differentiation UI with a \"Failed (not started)\" treatment distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Where `status.message.message_code` indicates an admission error, scheduling failure, or resource constraint, render \"Failed (not started)\" with an icon/color and label distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n- Distinct visual treatment per the PatternFly status pattern and UX-reviewed specifications.\n- Fallback behavior (part of the base failed-state rendering): when `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, a single \"Failed\" state is shown with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct visual treatment that differentiates it from a job that ran and then failed, measured by a label reflecting the failure type and an icon/color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, the row falls back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail (strategy's documented risk mitigation).\n- The additional state variant's icon/color specification is reviewed and approved by UX/design.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-7 [P2]: Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Depends on the state differentiation UI (this work extends its state badge/icon/color framework).\n- Gated by the investigation cataloging `status.message.message_code` values: if the values do not reliably distinguish pre-start from runtime failures across error scenarios, this feature is removed and the fallback (single \"Failed\" state with message text) stands.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49221,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af589b60cf509813","agent_id":"a76d34cd3e2df0381","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"ad4356f9-2b14-4b87-8a4c-e62ecde8690d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:55:38.520Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
