{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab27b16b974d3904","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n3\tepic_count: 6\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8005\n11\t\n12\t**Strategy**: EvalHub UI: Real-Time Evaluation Job Progress and State Visibility\n13\t\n14\t## Triage Outcome\n15\t\n16\tStrategy is S-sized, single active component (eval-hub-ui plugin), single implementing team (ODH Dashboard) — but the **genuine-unknowns escape condition applies**: the strategy's Open Questions table contains two unknowns flagged \"needs validation\" whose answers change what downstream epics do (mid-run availability of `status.benchmarks[]` determines whether the detail-polling layer and benchmark-progress display exist as specified; `status.message.message_code` values determine whether the pre-start/runtime failure distinction is implementable). Per Step 0, below-threshold does not apply; full decomposition performed.\n17\t\n18\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n19\t\n20\tStaff Engineer Input was parsed first and takes precedence. Logged overrides / resolutions:\n21\t\n22\t1. **Data availability constraint**: \"Assume we do not have any more data available to us other than what is already available from this API\" — no Server-side API extensions; all work builds on the two existing endpoints (`GET /evaluations/jobs`, `GET /evaluations/jobs/{id}`). The AI-generated Technical Approach already conforms; no divergence.\n23\t2. **Latency window open question resolved**: 10 seconds is sufficient for state-transition visibility.\n24\t3. **Page Visibility open question resolved**: yes, polling pauses when the tab is backgrounded.\n25\t4. **Concurrency model directed**: poll only jobs on the currently displayed table page; max 5 parallel detail fetches in round-robin; next cycle timer starts when all detail fetches complete; scalability out of scope for this release.\n26\t5. **Retry pattern directed**: replicate the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` exponential-backoff pattern with a non-blocking warning and last-successful-state preservation.\n27\t\n28\tThe two API-behavior open questions (benchmarks[] mid-run population; message_code value semantics) are **not** resolved by Staff Engineer Input and remain genuine unknowns → Investigation epics.\n29\t\n30\t## Component Mapping\n31\t\n32\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Notes |\n33\t|---|---|---|\n34\t| eval-hub-ui (odh-dashboard plugin) | AI Evaluations | Closest canonical name; all implementation epics. Architecture context file `eval-hub.md` / `odh-dashboard.md` confirm the plugin and BFF proxy exist in the platform. |\n35\t| odh-dashboard (BFF) | AI Core Dashboard | **Passive component** — \"verify BFF proxy passes through all response fields… no code change expected\", validated by the same team (ODH Dashboard) that owns the active work → modeled as an acceptance criterion on the detail-polling Implementation epic, not a separate epic (Step 2 passive-component rule). |\n36\t\n37\tBoth components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` → no onboarding chain (no repo-onboarding / license-validation / konflux-onboarding epics).\n38\t\n39\t## Epic List\n40\t\n41\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n42\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n43\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E001 | Validate mid-run availability of `status.benchmarks[]` in the EvalHub job detail API | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P0 |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E002 | Catalog `status.message.message_code` values for pre-start vs runtime evaluation job failures | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P2 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E003 | Detail-polling layer for in-progress evaluation jobs in the EvalHub UI | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E004 | Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P1 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E005 | State differentiation UI for the evaluation job list | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E006 | Pre-start vs runtime failure state distinction | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P2 |\n49\t\n50\t## Dependency DAG\n51\t\n52\t```mermaid\n53\tgraph TD\n54\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-8005-E001 Investigation: benchmarks[] mid-run] --> E003[RHAISTRAT-8005-E003 Detail-polling layer]\n55\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-8005-E004 Progress and elapsed-time display]\n56\t    E003 --> E004\n57\t    E002[RHAISTRAT-8005-E002 Investigation: message_code values] --> E006[RHAISTRAT-8005-E006 Failure distinction]\n58\t    E005[RHAISTRAT-8005-E005 State differentiation UI] --> E006\n59\t    E005 -. parallel .- E003\n60\t```\n61\t\n62\t## DAG Justification\n63\t\n64\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n65\t|---|---|---|\n66\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | If `status.benchmarks[]` is only populated on completion, mid-run detail polling yields no progress data and the polling layer's scope is rewritten (elapsed time falls back to `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint). True gate: `rewrite`. |\n67\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 | Benchmark-level progress (\"X/N complete\") is only displayable mid-run if `status.benchmarks[]` is populated during execution. True gate: `rewrite` (strategy's stated fallback — elapsed time becomes the primary progress indicator, benchmark count supplementary/absent mid-run). |\n68\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The progress display renders data delivered by the detail-polling hook and its round-robin scheduling; the consuming UI builds against the hook's data layer. |\n69\t| E002 → E006 | Rule 3 | If `message_code` values do not distinguish pre-start from runtime failures, the distinction feature does not exist (fallback: single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text, which is already in the base state UI). True gate: `remove`. |\n70\t| E005 → E006 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The failure-type distinction extends the state badge/icon/color framework built by the state differentiation UI. |\n71\t| E001 ∥ E002 ∥ E005 | Rules 14/15 | Independent questions and independent UI work on list-endpoint data (confirmed available); no shared artifacts. Parallel. |\n72\t| E003 ∥ E005 | Rule 15 | Same repo, different areas (data-fetching hook vs. state column rendering). Merge conflicts are coordination risk, not a dependency. |\n73\t\n74\t**Conditional-branch decision**: E001 has two bounded outcomes (populated mid-run vs. completion-only) and E002 has two (distinguishable vs. not). Neither produces structurally distinct downstream work: the negative outcomes are scope degradations with strategy-prescribed fallbacks (Risks table: elapsed-time-primary fallback; single-Failed-state fallback), i.e., rewrite/remove of the same epic rather than a different epic set. Modeled via `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact` on main-plan epics instead of branch files.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n77\t\n78\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n79\t|---|---|---|\n80\t| HLR-1 Auto-refresh mechanism for job list state transitions (list polling + detail polling) | P0 | E003 (detail-polling layer), E005 (state badge auto-update from existing 30s list polling) |\n81\t| HLR-2 Visual distinction queued/running/failed/completed from `status.state` | P0 | E005 |\n82\t| HLR-3 Non-blocking error handling during detail polling (backoff, inline warning, last state preserved) | P0 | E003 |\n83\t| HLR-4 Benchmark-level progress display from `status.benchmarks[]`, max-5 round-robin fetch | P1 | E003 (concurrency layer), E004 (display) |\n84\t| HLR-5 Elapsed time display from per-benchmark `started_at` | P1 | E004 |\n85\t| HLR-6 Page Visibility API pause/resume of polling | P1 | E003 |\n86\t| HLR-7 Pre-start vs runtime failure distinction via `status.message.message_code` | P2 | E006 |\n87\t\n88\tAll 7 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements.\n89\t\n90\t**Priority notes**: E001 is P0 because it gates E003, which carries P0 HLRs 1 and 3 (an epic blocking all P0 polling work is implicitly P0). E002 is P2 — it transitively enables only HLR-7 (P2). E004 is P1 (HLRs 4-5); it was **not** split from E003 by priority — the boundary is the architectural sub-system split (data-fetching layer vs. presentation), and HLR-4's fetch side is inseparable from E003's concurrency layer. HLR-7 (P2) is a separate epic not because of priority-split preference but because its existence is gated by E002 — bundling it into E005 would block P0 state work on the investigation.\n91\t\n92\t## Health Warnings\n93\t\n94\t1. **Human process gates on the P0 critical path (non-blocking)**: UXD Support (\"Required for progress indicator pattern, state icon/color specs\") and Architecture Review are \"_Pending human review_\" in the strategy's Prerequisites table. The state differentiation UI (P0) and progress display (P1) cannot complete their icon/color acceptance criteria without UXD sign-off. Also, the strategy's acceptance criteria are marked \"requires PM/Engineering validation\".\n95\t2. **Scope trap — performance (non-blocking)**: The NFR caps load at 5 concurrent detail requests per session, but the strategy explicitly defers scalability for high concurrent user counts and lists Performance Team Support as pending. The \"no network requests while backgrounded\" AC requires browser-dev-tools verification, and error-path ACs require simulating 5xx from the BFF — test setup effort is real but bounded.\n96\t3. **Priority inversion candidate (non-blocking)**: HLR-7 (P2) is the only HLR gated on E002; if the message_code catalog shows the distinction is achievable cheaply, it may warrant promotion — conversely the risk table's fallback (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text) means a negative E002 outcome costs little.\n97\t4. **Assumption risk folded into gates**: the assumption \"`status.benchmarks[]` populated during job execution — needs validation\" and \"`message_code` provides distinguishable values — needs validation\" are exactly the two gated investigations; degradation paths are strategy-prescribed.\n98\t\n99\t## Tiered Delivery\n100\t\n101\tNot applicable. All external/internal dependencies are status \"Exists\" (PatternFly, React Query, EvalHub Server endpoints, BFF proxy path, Module Federation infrastructure) — no dependency has uncertain timing, so no Tier 1/Tier 2 split is needed. Parallelism is achieved within the DAG: E002 and E005 run concurrently with the E001 → E003 → E004 chain.\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-873f54a69e88bd79","agent_id":"a4bfaf15eede9c69e","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"2f7b2277-1ed4-45f3-ad2d-8a38838ac645","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:57:50.912Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab27b16b974d3904","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
