{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89ab0ea49c724dcf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n3\ttitle: Catalog status.message.message_code values for pre-start vs runtime evaluation\n4\t  job failures\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P2\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Catalog status.message.message_code values for pre-start vs runtime evaluation job failures\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation catalogs the values the EvalHub Server returns in `status.message.message_code` for job failures, and determines whether they reliably distinguish pre-start failures (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource/quota constraints) from runtime failures (failures after execution has started). The strategy's optional pre-start vs runtime failure distinction (\"Failed (not started)\" vs \"Failed\") depends on this answer; the strategy explicitly flags it as an open question owned by the TrustyAI / EvalHub team (\"needs validation\").\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source for all sites that write `status.message.message_code` and enumerate the distinct values with their triggering conditions (admission, scheduling, quota, runtime errors).\n35\t- Cross-check against the published API reference for the job list and job detail endpoints.\n36\t- Where source reading is inconclusive, reproduce representative failure scenarios (may require a live cluster, e.g., quota-exceeded admission failure vs a failing benchmark runtime).\n37\t- Deliverable: a catalog table of `message_code` values mapped to failure phase (pre-start vs runtime), plus a verdict: distinguishable, partially distinguishable, or not distinguishable.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A written catalog enumerates the known `status.message.message_code` values and the failure phase each indicates.\n42\t- A clear verdict states whether the EvalHub UI can reliably render \"Failed (not started)\" distinct from \"Failed\" (runtime), including any ambiguous or absent-code scenarios.\n43\t- If the verdict is negative, the strategy's documented fallback is confirmed as the path: a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message.message` text displayed as supplementary detail.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- Enables HLR-7 [P2] (pre-start vs runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available) — the answer determines whether that feature is implemented or the fallback applies.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-873f54a69e88bd79","agent_id":"a4bfaf15eede9c69e","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"72338136-dc43-441e-9a7d-d430030be6d4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:57:55.576Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89ab0ea49c724dcf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
