{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bad20d2f6da1e086","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If status.benchmarks[] is only populated on job completion,\n16\t    benchmark X/N progress is unavailable mid-run: display elapsed time as the primary\n17\t    progress indicator (from resource.created_at when no benchmark has started) with\n18\t    the benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run, per the strategy''s documented\n19\t    risk mitigation.'\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic delivers the progress presentation for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps. It renders the data delivered by the detail-polling layer in the job table rows.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs: \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"`.\n46\t- Elapsed time display: computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (or `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started); formatted for display (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n47\t- Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n48\t- Per the strategy's risk mitigation, elapsed time is the primary progress indicator for all jobs (covering single-benchmark jobs where X/N is too coarse); the benchmark count is supplementary.\n49\t- State-cell/table-row layout changes to present progress alongside the state badge, following PatternFly progress and label components and the UX-specified progress indicator pattern.\n50\t- UX review of the progress indicator pattern (UXD support is listed as required for this in the strategy's prerequisites).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n55\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n56\t- For a single-benchmark job, the running state with elapsed time provides progress feedback (risk mitigation acceptance).\n57\t- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed and approved by UX/design against the dashboard design system.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-4 [P1]: Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (display half; the max-5 round-robin fetch is delivered by the detail-polling layer).\n62\t- HLR-5 [P1]: Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps obtained via detail polling.\n63\t\n64\t## Dependencies and Gating\n65\t\n66\t- Depends on the detail-polling layer (its UI renders data delivered by that hook and its round-robin scheduling).\n67\t- Gated by the investigation of mid-run `status.benchmarks[]` availability: if benchmark data is only populated on completion, this epic is rewritten to the strategy's fallback — elapsed time (from `resource.created_at` or list-endpoint data) as the primary progress indicator with the benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-873f54a69e88bd79","agent_id":"a4bfaf15eede9c69e","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"e856e39b-b2c3-4e1a-82d5-f2f77e194c85","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:58:00.550Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bad20d2f6da1e086","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92e75fe2b1322b00","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n3\ttitle: Detail-polling layer for in-progress evaluation jobs in the EvalHub UI\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: 'If status.benchmarks[] is only populated on job completion,\n15\t    mid-run detail polling yields no progress data: reduce or drop mid-run detail\n16\t    polling and compute elapsed time from resource.created_at in the list endpoint\n17\t    response, keeping top-level state display from the existing list polling.'\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Detail-polling layer for in-progress evaluation jobs in the EvalHub UI\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic delivers the new detail-polling data layer for the EvalHub Evaluations landing page in the RHOAI dashboard (eval-hub-ui plugin): a hook that identifies jobs on the currently displayed table page that are in a non-terminal state and fetches their detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) to obtain `status.benchmarks[]` for progress display. It implements the two-layer polling model directed by Staff Engineer input: the existing list-endpoint polling (30s, `useEvaluationJobs`) continues unchanged for top-level state, while this new layer runs on a 10-second cycle with round-robin concurrency control, retry-with-backoff error handling, and Page Visibility pausing.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- New detail-polling hook in the eval-hub-ui frontend that:\n44\t  - Tracks which jobs on the currently displayed table page (client-side pagination, default 20 rows, options 5/10/20) are in a non-terminal state, and updates the poll target set immediately when the page changes.\n45\t  - Dispatches detail fetches with a maximum of 5 concurrent requests in round-robin: as one request completes, the next pending in-progress job is fetched, keeping at most 5 in flight; when all detail fetches for the current page complete, a 10-second timer starts before the next cycle.\n46\t  - Only polls jobs visible on the current table page; jobs not in view are not polled.\n47\t- Retry-on-error per the autorag `usePipelineRunQuery` pattern: `placeholderData: (previousData) => previousData` to preserve the last successful response, exponential backoff with jitter up to the established max attempts, 4xx errors non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried.\n48\t- Non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert, \"warning\" variant) indicating status updates are temporarily unavailable while continuing to show the last successfully fetched data; a single failed detail request does not stop the round-robin (partial progress data is acceptable).\n49\t- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded and resumes on tab focus, triggering a single polling cycle immediately on resume.\n50\t- No Server-side API changes; all requests flow through the existing auth chain (kube-rbac-proxy → dashboard backend → eval-hub-ui plugin BFF → EvalHub Server) and existing `X-Tenant` multi-tenant scoping. No new auth paths.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling, when the frontend encounters a 5xx or network error on a detail fetch, then the last successfully fetched data for the affected job remains displayed, a non-blocking inline warning is shown, and the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job while the failed request retries with exponential backoff (up to 5 retries), measured by the UI continuing to render stale detail data and the warning Alert component being visible.\n55\t- Given the user navigates away from the browser tab, when the tab loses focus, then detail polling pauses and no further requests are made until the tab regains focus, at which point a single polling cycle is triggered immediately, measured by no network requests to the detail endpoint while the tab is backgrounded (verified via browser dev tools Network tab).\n56\t- Detail polling issues at most 5 concurrent requests per user session regardless of the number of in-progress jobs on the visible page, measured by observing the Network tab during a cycle with more than 5 in-progress jobs (round-robin dispatch).\n57\t- Only jobs on the currently displayed table page are polled; changing the page immediately retargets detail polling, measured by the set of detail-endpoint requests matching the visible rows.\n58\t- The odh-dashboard BFF proxy transparently passes through all response fields from the eval-hub-ui plugin backend for the detail endpoint (verification of existing behavior — no code change expected; transparent field passthrough is the existing pattern for Module Federation plugins).\n59\t- If the detail endpoint is unavailable or returns no benchmark data for a job, rows degrade gracefully to showing only top-level state from the list endpoint (backwards-compatibility NFR).\n60\t- The existing 30-second list-endpoint polling in `useEvaluationJobs` continues to function and coexists with the new detail-polling layer.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-1 [P0]: Auto-refresh mechanism using the existing list endpoint polling for top-level state and new detail endpoint polling for in-progress job progress (detail-polling half).\n65\t- HLR-3 [P0]: Non-blocking error handling during detail polling (last state preserved, inline warning, exponential backoff per the autorag pattern).\n66\t- HLR-6 [P1]: Polling pauses when the browser tab is not in the foreground and resumes immediately on focus.\n67\t- Partially enables HLR-4 [P1]: the max-5 concurrent round-robin fetch for in-progress jobs on the current table page (data delivery; display is handled by the progress display work).\n68\t\n69\t## Dependencies and Gating\n70\t\n71\t- Gated by the investigation of mid-run `status.benchmarks[]` availability: if the detail endpoint only populates benchmark data on completion, this epic's scope is rewritten — mid-run detail polling provides no progress data and elapsed time falls back to `resource.created_at` from the list endpoint.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-873f54a69e88bd79","agent_id":"a4bfaf15eede9c69e","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"37e5c805-183c-40d7-8d70-4c48e223ffa9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:58:00.552Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92e75fe2b1322b00","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
