{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-891f2259b7a5208c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: 'If status.benchmarks[] is only populated on job completion,\n16\t    benchmark X/N progress is unavailable mid-run: display elapsed time as the primary\n17\t    progress indicator (from resource.created_at when no benchmark has started) with\n18\t    the benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run, per the strategy''s documented\n19\t    risk mitigation.'\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 1\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Benchmark progress and elapsed-time display for running evaluation jobs\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tThis epic delivers the progress presentation for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps. It renders the data delivered by the detail-polling layer in the job table rows.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs: \"Benchmarks: X/N complete\" where X is the count of entries in `status.benchmarks[]` with `status: \"completed\"`.\n46\t- Elapsed time display: computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest `started_at` timestamp across all benchmarks (or `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started); formatted for display (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\").\n47\t- Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, the row shows only the top-level state from the list endpoint (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n48\t- Per the strategy's risk mitigation, elapsed time is the primary progress indicator for all jobs (covering single-benchmark jobs where X/N is too coarse); the benchmark count is supplementary.\n49\t- State-cell/table-row layout changes to present progress alongside the state badge, following PatternFly progress and label components and the UX-specified progress indicator pattern.\n50\t- UX review of the progress indicator pattern (UXD support is listed as required for this in the strategy's prerequisites).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the detail response.\n55\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response.\n56\t- For a single-benchmark job, the running state with elapsed time provides progress feedback (risk mitigation acceptance).\n57\t- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed and approved by UX/design against the dashboard design system.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- HLR-4 [P1]: Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (display half; the max-5 round-robin fetch is delivered by the detail-polling layer).\n62\t- HLR-5 [P1]: Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps obtained via detail polling.\n63\t\n64\t## Dependencies and Gating\n65\t\n66\t- Depends on the detail-polling layer (its UI renders data delivered by that hook and its round-robin scheduling).\n67\t- Gated by the investigation of mid-run `status.benchmarks[]` availability: if benchmark data is only populated on completion, this epic is rewritten to the strategy's fallback — elapsed time (from `resource.created_at` or list-endpoint data) as the primary progress indicator with the benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fb63b737b075928","agent_id":"a4271d12c344d366e","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"ac9427ba-b33c-427d-b402-2a87580901e5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:03:33.494Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-891f2259b7a5208c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
