{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-997b00b8bdc7d789","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate mid-run availability of status.benchmarks[] in the EvalHub job detail\n4\t  API\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate mid-run availability of status.benchmarks[] in the EvalHub job detail API\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves whether the EvalHub Server's job detail endpoint (`GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}`) populates the `status.benchmarks[]` array — per-benchmark status entries with `started_at`/`completed_at` — while a job is still running, or only after completion. The strategy's benchmark-level progress display (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") and mid-run elapsed-time computation depend on this answer. The strategy explicitly flags this as an open question owned by the TrustyAI / EvalHub team (\"needs validation\"), and Staff Engineer direction constrains the solution to data already available from the existing API.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source (upstream repository, evaluation-jobs status handling) and the published API reference for `GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}` to determine when `status.benchmarks[]` entries are written relative to job state transitions (pending → running → completed/failed).\n35\t- Determine whether per-benchmark `started_at` is available before the first benchmark completes (needed for mid-run elapsed time).\n36\t- Where source reading is inconclusive, empirically observe the detail-endpoint response for a running evaluation job (may require a live cluster running an evaluation job).\n37\t- Deliverable: a short findings report stating (a) whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated mid-run, (b) which per-benchmark fields are present at each job state, and (c) the recommended display consequence: benchmark-progress display as planned, or the strategy's fallback (elapsed time as primary progress indicator, benchmark count supplementary or absent mid-run).\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A written findings report answers, with evidence (source file references and/or captured API responses): \"Is `status.benchmarks[]` populated with per-benchmark status entries while a job is still running, or only after completion?\"\n42\t- The report states which fallback (if any) the EvalHub UI progress display must adopt.\n43\t- The TrustyAI / EvalHub team and the ODH Dashboard team sign off on the conclusion.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- Enables HLR-1 [P0] (auto-refresh with detail-endpoint progress data), HLR-4 [P1] (benchmark-level progress display), HLR-5 [P1] (elapsed time from per-benchmark `started_at`) — the answers determine whether these are implemented as specified or degraded per the strategy's risk fallback.\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03952b5ed3666ea","agent_id":"ad9470eb955510244","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"35be04e4-b34f-42ed-bd41-76922fe135dd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:33.380Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-997b00b8bdc7d789","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005"}
