{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-851012aaf99a86fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n3\ttitle: State differentiation UI for the evaluation job list\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# State differentiation UI for the evaluation job list\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the visual state differentiation for the EvalHub Evaluations landing page job table: distinct labels, PatternFly status icons, and color treatments for queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states, derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field (available for all jobs without detail fetch). It also ensures state badges update automatically from the existing 30-second list polling so state transitions are visible without manual browser refresh.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- State mapping driven by the list endpoint's `status.state`: Queued/Pending (state `pending`), Running (active execution), Failed (failure, with `status.message` providing error context), Completed (state `completed`).\n38\t- Each state rendered with a distinct PatternFly status icon, color, and label per the dashboard design system's status pattern.\n39\t- The job list row's state label updates automatically as the existing list-endpoint polling (30s) returns new state — no manual page refresh required.\n40\t- UX/design review of state icon and color specifications (UXD support is listed as required in the strategy's prerequisites).\n41\t- No change to the list endpoint or its polling cadence; purely additive rendering work.\n42\t- Coordination note: the state badge renders in the same EvaluationsTable state-cell/table-row surface that the progress-display workstream modifies; the two workstreams run in parallel by design. Coordinate the shared state-cell layout and branch sequencing with the progress-display workstream to avoid merge conflicts on the shared table surface.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Given an evaluation job is queued/pending (not yet started), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct \"Queued\" label and visual treatment that is visually distinguishable from \"Running\" and \"Failed\" states, measured by distinct icon, color, and label text per the PatternFly status pattern.\n47\t- Given an evaluation job transitions from running to complete, when the user is on the Evaluations landing page without manually refreshing the browser, then the status update is visible within the list endpoint's polling interval (30 seconds) for the state badge, measured by the job list row updating its state label automatically.\n48\t- Given a job has failed, the row renders the \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text available as error context.\n49\t- State icon/color specifications are reviewed and approved by UX/design against the dashboard design system.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-2 [P0]: Visual distinction between queued/pending, actively running, failed, and completed states with distinct labels, icons, and color treatments derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field.\n54\t- HLR-1 [P0] (list-polling half): state transitions visible without manual refresh from the existing list endpoint polling.\n55\t\n56\t## Dependencies and Gating\n57\t\n58\t- No gating dependencies: the list endpoint's `status.state` and `status.message` fields are confirmed available for all jobs; this work proceeds in parallel with the detail-polling investigation and data-layer work.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03952b5ed3666ea","agent_id":"ad9470eb955510244","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"6536e29f-d0b0-4eb7-a6d7-a10cb99d1cc0","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:42.624Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-851012aaf99a86fd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005"}
