{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8aa79a9da6366c75","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E006\n3\ttitle: Pre-start vs runtime failure state distinction\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If message_code values do not reliably distinguish pre-start\n16\t    from runtime failures across error scenarios, remove the distinction and render\n17\t    a single Failed state with status.message text as supplementary detail (the strategy's\n18\t    documented fallback).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 3\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Pre-start vs runtime failure state distinction\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tThis epic delivers the optional distinction between jobs that failed before execution started (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource constraints) and jobs that ran and then failed, using `status.message.message_code` where available. It extends the state differentiation UI with a \"Failed (not started)\" treatment distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Where `status.message.message_code` indicates an admission error, scheduling failure, or resource constraint, render \"Failed (not started)\" with an icon/color and label distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n45\t- Distinct visual treatment per the PatternFly status pattern and UX-reviewed specifications.\n46\t- Fallback behavior (part of the base failed-state rendering): when `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, a single \"Failed\" state is shown with `status.message` text as supplementary detail.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct visual treatment that differentiates it from a job that ran and then failed, measured by a label reflecting the failure type and an icon/color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n51\t- Where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent, the row falls back to the single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail (strategy's documented risk mitigation).\n52\t- The additional state variant's icon/color specification is reviewed and approved by UX/design.\n53\t\n54\t## HLR Traceability\n55\t\n56\t- HLR-7 [P2]: Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available.\n57\t\n58\t## Dependencies and Gating\n59\t\n60\t- Depends on the state differentiation UI (this work extends its state badge/icon/color framework).\n61\t- Gated by the investigation cataloging `status.message.message_code` values: if the values do not reliably distinguish pre-start from runtime failures across error scenarios, this feature is removed and the fallback (single \"Failed\" state with message text) stands.\n62\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03952b5ed3666ea","agent_id":"ad9470eb955510244","session_id":"1da74765-444a-4960-9d12-3d9467f39461","uuid":"caa20fcb-972a-4ac4-a1f8-7f03e1123db4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:05:43.646Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8aa79a9da6366c75","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005"}
