ce (2/2)\n\nDiagram/frontmatter cross-check: every edge in the summary DAG (E001→E003, E001→E004, E003→E004, E002→E006, E005→E006) has a matching entry in the target epic's `dependencies` frontmatter, and vice versa — no extra or missing frontmatter dependencies. Arrows run dependency → dependent per convention. No cycles. All referenced epics exist. No branch files are used, and no main-plan epic depends on a branch node.\n\nNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics exist (both components present in architecture context), so the mandated-parallel rule-7/8/10 pairings are vacuously satisfied.\n\nEdges are justified: Investigation gating edges (E001→E003/E004, E002→E006) are true gates with structurally meaningful outcomes; E003→E004 and E005→E006 are framework→consumer edges. Parallel-eligible work is not serialized: E005 (P0 state UI) runs parallel to the E001→E003 chain, and the shared EvaluationsTable surface between E004 and E005 is correctly modeled as a Rule 15 coordination risk (merge conflicts), not a dependency — both epics carry explicit coordination notes. The E001→E004 edge is redundant given E001→E003→E004, but redundant transitive listing is harmless and required for the `gated_by` direct-dependency check.\n\nCritical path 3 slightly exceeds the S-size heuristic (1-2), but is justified: the genuine-unknowns escape means the gated investigation chain (E001 before the data layer it gates) legitimately lengthens the path. Minor observation only.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nTeam tuples separate correctly: both Investigation epics are owned by TrustyAI / EvalHub (the strategy's designated owners of the two open questions), all four Implementation epics by ODH Dashboard. No epic spans multiple teams or bundles work across components. The passive odh-dashboard BFF component (\"verify passthrough, no code change expected\") is correctly modeled as an acceptance criterion on E003 rather than a separate epic.\n\nNo scope duplication: E003 (data-fetch layer) vs. E004 (progress display) split along the architectural axis; E005 (base state badges) vs. E006 (failure-type extension) are distinct increments of the same framework with a dependency edge, not duplicated work. No work-product type mixing (no content authoring bundled with code). Each epic is well within a single sprint for an S-sized, single-plugin frontend effort.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n\nBoth Investigations genuinely resolve uncertainty that changes downstream structure: E001's outcome rewrites E003/E004 (mid-run benchmarks[] availability), E002's outcome removes E006 (message_code distinguishability) — both are strategy-flagged \"needs validation\" unknowns, not scheduling dependencies. Both have downstream dependents and produce concrete findings deliverables.\n\nGating metadata is complete and correct: E003, E004 (gated_by E001) and E006 (gated_by E002) each have `gate_failure_impact` with both `action` and `fallback_approach` populated with strategy-prescribed fallbacks; every `gated_by` target appears in that epic's direct `dependencies`; every epic listing an Investigation in `dependencies` has `gated_by` set. E005 correctly has no gating (its data fields are confirmed available). No misclassifications.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nSignal fields are type-appropriate: E001/E002 carry `investigation_signals` (5-signal rubric); E003–E006 carry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric). No cross-type contamination. All six ai-signals rationale files exist, and every frontmatter value matches its rationale entry.\n\nSpot-checks against strategy content hold: E003 `open_questions: -1` (gated on unresolved mid-run benchmarks[] question) vs. E005 `open_questions: +1` (list-endpoint fields confirmed available — the genuinely unknown piece is scoped to E006); E006 `change_specificity: 0` (triggering message_code values unknown pending the catalog) is exactly right; `human_process_gates: -1` across implementation epics